# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ThinkTrace AI — environment configuration
#
# Everything here is OPTIONAL. With no .env.local at all the app runs in
# demo mode: an in-memory store plus a deterministic analyzer, fully
# functional and clearly labelled as such in the UI.
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in what you have:  cp .env.example .env.local
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Supabase ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set BOTH to enable real accounts, persistence and Realtime responses.
# Find them in your Supabase project under Settings → API.
# Run supabase/schema.sql in the SQL editor first.
# These two are exposed to the browser by design — the anon key is safe to
# publish and is protected by the row-level security policies in schema.sql.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Language model ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set ONE to enable live misconception analysis. Read only on the server and
# never sent to the browser. Anthropic takes precedence if both are present.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional model overrides. The default is Claude Opus 5.
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# How hard the model works per request: low | medium | high | xhigh | max.
# Defaults to "medium" because a student is watching a spinner. Raise it if you
# care more about the depth of the analysis than the wait.
# ANTHROPIC_EFFORT=medium

# Abort an analysis call after this many milliseconds and fall back to the
# demo analyzer, so a slow model never leaves a screen hanging.
# LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=60000

# Optional API base overrides — for a corporate gateway, a proxy, or a local
# mock during testing. Default to the providers' own endpoints.
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com
